  <h1 class="page-h1">Florida Quitclaim Deed Form: Requirements You Actually Need to Know</h1>

  <p class="last-updated">Updated August 7, 2026 using the primary authorities cited below.</p>

  <!-- Intro -->
  <p>
    Florida's quitclaim deed requirements include a two-witness rule that most states don't have — and
    it's the single most common reason Florida deeds are rejected at the county recorder's office. Not
    the notary — the second witness. Florida §689.01 requires two subscribing witnesses for execution,
    in addition to the acknowledgment required under §695.03 for recording. Miss that, and the county
    clerk rejects the deed at recording, no refund on the doc stamp tax you already paid.
  </p>

  <!-- Primary CTA: DeedForm -->
